{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"c3d263ab8b32cc5d091db5aa21188c5ca88989efec8c712ff9585bfa3ec613f6","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate sidecar","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","fix_unit_key()","_norm_location()","_norm_claim()","norm_id","build_payload","group_id","is_primary","group_criteria"],"problem_keywords":["blocking findings","multi-criterion deduplication","finding grouping","inflated block wall","fix-unit consolidation","criterion-scoped normalization"],"propositions":["A single plan defect surfaces as N duplicate blocking findings when multiple independent criteria cite the same location and claim, inflating agent block tallies and distorting per-criterion counts for calibration.","The existing norm_id helper is criterion-scoped (its hash includes the sorted criteria list), so two findings with identical text but different criteria cannot be grouped using norm_id alone.","Blocking findings sharing the same normalized location and normalized claim (criteria-excluded) must be grouped into one fix-unit, with all N findings retained in verdict['blocking'], exactly one marked is_primary=True, and group_id/group_criteria stamped on each.","The CLI renderer must suppress non-primary findings in grouped blocks and display a '(+N co-criteria: <union>)' suffix on the primary, while library/MCP consumers see the full unfiltered stamped list.","Grouped findings retain decision=block and gate semantics unchanged; grouping is a metadata-only stamp operation applied after verdict production and before sidecar emit, with group_id/is_primary/group_criteria explicitly added to _slim() persistence."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785820043245268178,"uuid":"ed8c3bfa-140c-4fc9-894c-1f0eeeba68f0"}